From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The frame limiter sleeps to 200 us before its deadline

From deurefdfgdf's BKFT fork of ARMSX2 (4bdbd0a23e, the limiter part only).
VMManager::Internal::Throttle slept whole milliseconds minus one and spun
the rest, up to about 2 ms at every call, twice a frame, whenever a game
runs at full speed: no speed for it, only a core kept busy. It now sleeps
until 200 us before the deadline and spins only that (BKFT_LIMITER_SPIN_US
sets the margin; a negative value gives the old sleep back).

On an RG52 Mini, The Sopranos' disc in the BIOS's browser at full speed (PAL,
50 fps), 40 s, four runs each: the EE thread 46% of a core before, 39% after;
the whole process 81% against 74%; the same 50.48 fps.

diff --git a/pcsx2/VMManager.cpp b/pcsx2/VMManager.cpp
index 417a538..d39478f 100644
--- a/pcsx2/VMManager.cpp
+++ b/pcsx2/VMManager.cpp
@@ -3095,6 +3095,20 @@ void VMManager::ResetFrameLimiter()
 	s_limiter_frame_start = GetCPUTicks();
 }
 
+#if defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)
+// BKFT: how far before the limiter's deadline the sleep ends, in CPU ticks: BKFT_LIMITER_SPIN_US
+// microseconds, 200 by default; a negative value gives -1, the old whole-milliseconds sleep.
+static s64 BkftLimiterMarginTicks()
+{
+	static const s64 s_margin = [] {
+		const char* value = std::getenv("BKFT_LIMITER_SPIN_US");
+		const long long us = (value && value[0] != '\0') ? std::strtoll(value, nullptr, 10) : 200;
+		return (us < 0) ? s64(-1) : static_cast<s64>((static_cast<u64>(us) * GetTickFrequency()) / 1000000u);
+	}();
+	return s_margin;
+}
+#endif
+
 void VMManager::Internal::Throttle(bool vsync_start)
 {
 	if (s_target_speed == 0.0f || s_use_vsync_for_timing)
@@ -3146,16 +3160,30 @@ void VMManager::Internal::Throttle(bool vsync_start)
 		return;
 	}
 
